  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.0.8\"\n\npackage:\n  name: yprov4wfs\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/y/yprov4wfs/yprov4wfs-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 9e05b9a84f6a1cd240880a43fe8212f2e26818e54b2e5746abe4e1b9d579c152\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script:\n    env:\n      # setup.py reads README.md without an explicit encoding, so Python falls\n      # back to the locale encoding. That is cp1252 on Windows, which cannot\n      # decode the UTF-8 README. Reported upstream:\n      # https://github.com/HPCI-Lab/yProv4WFs\n      PYTHONUTF8: \"1\"\n    content: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - setuptools >=42\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - yprov4wfs\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n\nabout:\n  summary: A module for tracking the provenance of a workflow using a Workflow Management System.\n  # NOTE TO ANYONE UPDATING THIS RECIPE: the license changed after 0.0.8.\n  # 0.0.8 is GPL-3.0 consistently (LICENSE, setup.py and PKG-INFO all agree).\n  # Upstream relicensed to Apache-2.0 on 2025-11-07, after 0.0.8 was released,\n  # so any version newer than 0.0.8 needs `license` updated here.\n  # Be careful: that relicense only touched the LICENSE file. As of tag v0.1.2\n  # the LICENSE is Apache-2.0 but pyproject.toml and setup.py still declare\n  # GPLv3, so the two disagree. Check both before changing this field.\n  # (Newer versions are also GitHub-only -- PyPI has had nothing past 0.0.8\n  # since 2025-04-30 -- and declare version 0.0.9 even at tag v0.1.2.)\n  license: GPL-3.0-only\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  homepage: https://github.com/HPCI-Lab/yProv4WFs\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - martinRenou\n    - arjxn-py\n",
